Z||000000||fiero87||10-19-2000||10:31 AM||||Hello fellow list members,<P>I have been fallowing this thread about the sunbird turbo for the last week, and personally don't want to see this issue go away.  I happend to have an 87 coupe that could use a new engine, and i absolutly love turbo cars.  I already have a dodge daytona, and all my friends drive diamond stars(Eclipse, Laser, Talon)  And there is no way i'm going to be able to afford a design one systems kit for my GT.  So what is the chance of someone actually constructing a kit for this engine?  I'm less mechanicly inlcined that i'd like to be, otherwise i'd try to.  But through simple logic, (could be very wrong) these engines were in grand am's too.  And the grandam also had the tech 4 as an option.  Thus in theroy wouldn't this be sorta an easy swap?  Would the 5sp trans bolt to the new engine?  What about the mounts?  I know wiring would be a nightmare, but thats what we have Chris West, Ace, and other conversion places for.  This engine is lightweight, and very easy to find in yards, At least in my area(Midwest).  I'm sure with an intercooler and a few other light mods we could get some decent power from it.  Also, I wonder if redshift(company that orgianally did the coversion) would still have some record of how they did it?  You'd think somone would have to?  Anyway this is just my thoughts, and i hope i don't get flamed for this, but i really think this could be the next 3800SC swap.  Any thoughts, Feel free to email me or post to the fourm.  Thanks<BR>Tim<BR>86 GT<BR>87 Coupe||||reg||5
Z||000001||AdoRe||10-19-2000||12:23 PM||||I am currently rebulding a 2.0 turbo and it is a very easy engine to work with much better than the original 2.0 the turbo<BR>has diffrent piston,blanced crank,multi-port injection,diffrent valves spring.ect<BR>the engine is also very lightweight and almost every transmison will bolt right to it! this is a very intresting swap and when you put an intercooler weve put one from a sprint turbo and it becomes a real Civic Killer with bigger injectors and larger throttle body it is very able to put out 200hp from 2.0.<BR>the only know problem with the engine is the head gasket just torque the head when the engine is hot evrey 6month it is bulit proof!<BR>thanks||||reg||14
